WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.290
This is a very interesting new poll.

00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:07.770
I think about 10 people in the last 12 or
so hours sent this to me and they want me

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:08.900
to talk about it.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.900
So let's do it.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:15.140
There's a question about the 2020 Democratic
primary that many people find important and

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.140
some don't.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:23.000
And the question is, who of the Democratic
candidates would attract the most Trump voters?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.850
People who voted Trump in 2016 who of the
Democratic candidates would have the highest

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.530
appeal to that group of people?

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:34.860
And I've said before, I don't think that the
way to win 2020 is by convincing Trump voters

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:36.149
to vote for a democrat.

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:41.329
Okay, we're much better off winning on turnout
since half the country doesn't vote.

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:45.989
Let's just make sure that people who are already
on our side understand the importance of voting

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:46.989
and choose to vote.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:51.920
It is much easier to register 10 people to
vote than to convince a Trump is to vote for

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.139
a Democrat in 2020 but that being said, if
there is a candidate that is going to pull

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:02.359
way more Trumpists over to our side, it would
be important to know that.

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:03.850
And I would want to know that.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.770
And then I can think about, well, is that
something that I want to consider when I'm

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:09.960
deciding who to support in the Democratic
primary?

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:15.390
So yesterday people started sending me a page
from a recent economist you gov poll, which

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:22.689
seems to say Bernie Sanders followed by Andrew
Yang would pull the most 2016 Trump voters

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:23.790
to our side.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.840
So let's look at the poll numbers first.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.799
And remember, I am just the Messenger here.

00:01:27.799 --> 00:01:29.659
I am not arguing that this is the case.

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:33.810
I am merely showing you data from a poll,
which says this is the case.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:38.920
So looking at this, you'll notice that from
the people pulled who voted Trump in 2016

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.049
this is the furthest right column on your
screen.

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:47.149
14% say they'd vote Bernie and 10% say they'd
vote for Andrew Yang.

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:50.050
And then in third place, 9% say they'd vote
for Pete Buddha judge.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.759
So this is very interesting, the idea being
that Bernie Sanders is the candidate who would

00:01:53.759 --> 00:02:00.570
most bring Trump voters to the democratic
side and that Andrew Yang is the second highest,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:04.590
uh, candidate in terms of who would bring
Trump voters over to the democratic side.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:09.250
Now this is very interesting, but if we want
to really evaluate this, we have to look at

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.970
the details because there are math questions
about this and there are also political questions

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:14.970
about those.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:15.970
Let's start with the math.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:22.490
You will notice at the bottom right of the
image that it says unweighted and 41 this

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:28.270
means that the sample size of Trump voters,
for this question, unweighted was 41 people

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:34.990
out of the 41 Trump voters included in this
sample, 14% said they'd vote Bernie and 10%

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.140
for Yang.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:41.260
That's six people saying that they voted for
Trump in 2016 but would vote Bernie in in

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.560
2020 and four for Yang.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:48.880
These are not exactly the large numbers around
which I would necessarily be taking away too

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.410
much, but that doesn't mean that the data
is not still interesting.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:56.000
Now, more importantly, there's a political
question here.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.710
Just because Trump is prefer Bernie and Yang
over whoever else, that doesn't mean they

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.800
would actually vote for them over Trump.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:11.081
The question was, if the Democratic presidential
primary in your state were held today, who

00:03:11.081 --> 00:03:12.310
would you vote for?

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.310
Okay.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:18.180
Just because a Trumpist voting in the dem
primary would choose Bernie or Yang doesn't

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.410
mean they would choose Bernie or Yang over
Trump in the general election.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.370
That's a really important thing to understand.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:30.970
The other element of this is that you might
say, wait a second, why would Trumpists be

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.970
voting?

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:36.640
Why would Trump is who voted for Trump in
2016 even be voting in the 2020 Democratic

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:37.770
primary?

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:43.120
That's another relevant question because based
on how it is in the poll, the 41 people answering

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:49.960
that question are 2016 Trump voters who say
they will be voting in the 2020 Democratic

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:55.720
primary when the sample is 41 and we don't
know if there are people who are Republicans

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:00.360
in a state with an open primary who are going
to vote in the Democratic primary.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.570
We don't know if some of them are lying about
having voted for Donald Trump.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.850
We don't know if some of them are lying about
planning to vote in the 2020 primary.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:12.550
The point is when you've got just 41 people,
if just three people here lied, uh, then the

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:15.570
numbers all of a sudden become much less significant.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:20.290
Now, all of that being said, to go back to
the initial question, with all of the things

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:27.660
that we can consider and thinking about which
2020 a democratic candidate we should be supporting,

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:33.060
I actually do not believe that picking a candidate,
because a slightly higher portion of Trumpists

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:37.810
would consider voting for them as a good strategy
because we are going to have to win despite

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:44.280
the Trumpists, not by convincing them and
big picture, particularly since a preference

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.840
for one Democrat over another does not tell
us that they would even vote for that person

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.470
over Trump in the general election.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:57.500
I don't know that the right approach is to
be looking at polls and saying, well, 14%

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.110
would vote Bernie, 10% would vote Yang.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.270
I'm going to make a decision on that basis.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.630
I think we should be supporting the progressive
candidate.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:09.500
I'm a progressive, so I want to look for a
progressive candidate whose policy ideas most

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.620
match ours period.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.180
And then once we have a democratic nominee
selected, we should be working on get out

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.180
the vote.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:17.180
Half the country doesn't vote.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:21.260
Let's find people who are already sympathetic
to our political beliefs, but who may not

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:26.020
be planning to vote and get them to register
and vote.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:30.370
Convincing Trumpists either by calculating
the Democratic nominee that would most appeal

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:35.310
to them or just like debating Trumpist and
trying to beat them over the head with logic

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.310
into voting for a democrat.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:40.520
That is not the strategy that will remove
Trump in 2020.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:44.090
If you disagree with me, I'm open to having
my mind changed.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.310
Uh, follow me on Instagram at Davidson Dot

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:50.639
pacman and tell me exactly where and why you
disagree with me.

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:53.030
You can also follow the David Pakman show
